From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: sram: qcom: allow OCMEM interconnect control

Allow standard ICC control of the OCMEM memory clock. Keep a minimal
allocator-access vote and let the GPU OPP client request the factory
bandwidth. With ICC, do not issue the independent legacy 1 kHz RPM clock
vote, which can overwrite the aggregated vote for the same resource.
Preserve legacy operation when no interconnect path is present.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sram/qcom,ocmem.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sram/qcom,ocmem.yaml
index 61c784ef7..9a808a53b 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sram/qcom,ocmem.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sram/qcom,ocmem.yaml
@@ -41,6 +41,13 @@ properties:
       - const: core
       - const: iface
 
+  interconnects:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description: OCMEM memory clock bandwidth path
+
+  interconnect-names:
+    const: memory
+
   '#address-cells':
     const: 1
 
